o the union leader in  New Hampshire as well as the Keene paper  and the Quad Cities New York Times all  of them make that case for me that I'm  someone that can bring our party  together and bring people with me and I  think that's very very important and  I've just got to believe despite the  fact that three days before the Iowa  caucus I never thought I'd be here in  the Capitol I thought I'd be out with my  competitors doing my job I just don't  think that people are gonna hold that  against me I think my experience passing  over a hundred bills by working across  the aisle more than  one in the Senate running for president  I think that's going to matter I just  have a minute left you mentioned the  debates there was a ruling by the DNC  that seems to open the door to Mike  Bloomberg qualifying for at least one  debate coming up are you okay with that  yes I think that when you have got  someone that is running all those ads  all over the place including a Super  Bowl ad I think that it is better to  have that person debating in the case of  Mayor Bloomberg than outside just  spending a ton of money because I want  to make the case to America that I'd be  the best one to lead the ticket and I'd  rather debate him than have him outdo me  on the airwaves and what happens if  Bernie Sanders wins Iowa goes on to win  New Hampshire what happens to the party  I would say that this is a long long  primary and there are many steps along  the way I continue to believe that is  best to have someone leading our ticket  that for instance in my case I don't  support Medicare for all  I read the bill I never got on it I'm  not gonna kick 149 million Americans off  their current health insurance which is  what that bill says on page eight I  believe with education I know that free  college for all sounds good on a bumper  sticker but I think the best thing is to  match our education system with our  economy and when you do that you see we  have over a million openings forecast  for home health care workers over a  hundred thousand openings for  electricians we're not going to have a  shortage of Sports Marketing degrees  we're gonna have a shortage of plumbers  so this means investment in K through 12  one in two-year degrees and then  doubling the programs for college  students I think those are plans and not  pipe drinked they're progressive but  they are practical the center Klobuchar  we appreciate your time I'm heading to  Iowa tomorrow we'll see them when you  get there we'll see if I'm there you  maybe be there but I plan on being there  at least by Sunday okay senator thanks  thank you
 

